 #:seon.task{:name "the-user-prompt-stop-sequence-cuts-the-models-first-form"
             :kind :function
             :intent "The transcript shows every exchange as `user=> form` and the model row stops on \"user=>\" (`:seon.config.ai/stop`), so a model that writes its next form the way the transcript shows it is cut before the form: the first deepseek-flash pass of the live-agent run (agent live-flash, default 6cc5dbbb4, 2026-10-08) ended after prose and an opening ```clojure fence, 78 completion tokens, finish reason stop, and answered 'Your reply had no form'. Done when the prompt marker the transcript teaches and the stop sequence never collide: a model reply that writes `user=> (f)` evaluates (f)."
